# Rank 1386 / CVE-2020-7611 (GHSA-694p-xrhg-x3wm): Micronaut's own Netty header
# type, io.micronaut.http.netty.NettyHttpHeaders, built its backing store with
# Netty's header validation switched off:
#
#   public NettyHttpHeaders() {
#       this.nettyHeaders = new DefaultHttpHeaders(false);
#       this.conversionService = ConversionService.SHARED;
#   }
#
# DefaultHttpHeaders(boolean validate) is documented as "validate -- validate
# header names and values", and that validator is what rejects CR, LF and NUL in
# a header value and separators in a header name. With it off, any string an
# application hands to MutableHttpHeaders.add/set -- a forwarded cookie, a
# tenant id, a query parameter copied onto an outbound request -- is written to
# the wire verbatim, so a value carrying "\r\n" terminates the header block
# early and injects a second message. Fix 9d1eff5c8d is one line, dropping the
# argument so the no-arg constructor's default validation applies.
#
# The attacker is not a Micronaut committer and not the author of any particular
# application: it is whoever controls a string that an application built on
# Micronaut puts into a header, and the framework is what decides whether that
# string is validated. Micronaut's HTTP client and its mutable server responses
# both route through this one type, so a single constructor argument removed the
# guarantee for every application on the framework at once -- request smuggling
# against the upstream the client talks to (CWE-444), response splitting toward
# the browser (CWE-113). That is what makes the fact worth detecting where it
# is: the same call in one application would compromise only that application,
# but the detectable fact is identical in both, which is why the binding names
# the Netty constructor and not anything about Micronaut.
#
# FIXED. Nothing is tainted here and there is no path to trace -- the weakness
# is a control switched off at construction, exactly the shape
# code.CertValidationDisabled already occupies for TLS -- so a taint rule can
# never reach it. code.HttpHeaderValidationDisabled and rule VYQL-INJ-247
# (CWE-113, CWE-444) judge it, and the Java binding keys on the documented
# constructor argument: the classes it names are those whose only boolean
# parameter is the validation flag in every overload, so a false literal in the
# argument list cannot be anything else. HttpClientCodec and
# DefaultFullHttpResponse are deliberately excluded because each takes a second,
# unrelated boolean (failOnMissingResponse, singleFieldHeaders) that a
# positional guess would misread. The builder spelling
# (Http2FrameCodecBuilder.validateHeaders(false),
# HttpDecoderConfig.setValidateHeaders(false)) is covered by name rather than by
# position.
#
# The predicate is callee.method, not callee.path, and that is load-bearing. A
# Java call node's path carries its whole receiver chain, so
# `new DefaultHttpHeaders().setBoolean(name, false)` resolves to
# DefaultHttpHeaders.setBoolean and `builder.validateHeaders(true)
# .autoAckSettingsFrame(false)` to ...validateHeaders.autoAckSettingsFrame.
# Because a path match is segment-aware anywhere in the path, not only at its
# end, `callee.path ~= "DefaultHttpHeaders"` accepted both of those and read the
# following call's arguments -- two findings on two safe lines, measured. Both
# shapes are pinned as reject cases below.
#
# Measured bounded (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB, --cache off), every count the
# same across three runs. micronaut-core http-netty + http-server-netty +
# http-client at 9d1eff5c8d^: 25 findings without the binding, 26 with it, the
# extra one VYQL-INJ-247 at
# http-netty/src/main/java/io/micronaut/http/netty/NettyHttpHeaders.java:56; at
# 9d1eff5c8d, 25 and no VYQL-INJ-247. Whole micronaut-core (2670 java, 1188
# groovy, 286 kotlin): 237 findings at 9d1eff5c8d^ with exactly one
# VYQL-INJ-247, the CVE line, and 236 with none at 9d1eff5c8d. The four other
# DefaultHttpHeaders constructions in the tree (HttpResponseEncoder,
# NettyServerWebSocketUpgradeHandler, EmptyHttpRequest, EmptyHttpResponse) pass
# no argument and none is reported.
#
# netty itself, codec-http + codec-http2, reports 35 VYQL-INJ-247 and every one
# is under src/test: DefaultHttpHeadersTest, ReadOnlyHttpHeadersTest,
# DefaultHttp2HeadersDecoderTest and the rest exercise the non-validating path
# deliberately, and each reported line is a literal validate=false construction
# rather than a misread. Nothing under src/main is reported. Three unrelated
# Java trees totalling 2582 files -- logging-log4j2, the Jenkins git and
# mercurial plugins -- report zero. No identifier this binding names appears
# anywhere in the OWASP Java Benchmark corpus, and the full spec suite passes at
# 4868 specs.

test "rank1386: a framework header type whose backing Netty header store is constructed with validation disabled"
  lang java
  file http-netty/src/main/java/io/micronaut/http/netty/NettyHttpHeaders.java
  expect VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  package io.micronaut.http.netty;

  import io.micronaut.core.convert.ConversionService;
  import io.micronaut.http.MutableHttpHeaders;
  import io.netty.handler.codec.http.DefaultHttpHeaders;

  public class NettyHttpHeaders implements MutableHttpHeaders {

      io.netty.handler.codec.http.HttpHeaders nettyHeaders;
      final ConversionService<?> conversionService;

      public NettyHttpHeaders(io.netty.handler.codec.http.HttpHeaders nettyHeaders, ConversionService conversionService) {
          this.nettyHeaders = nettyHeaders;
          this.conversionService = conversionService;
      }

      public NettyHttpHeaders() {
          this.nettyHeaders = new DefaultHttpHeaders(false);
          this.conversionService = ConversionService.SHARED;
      }

      @Override
      public MutableHttpHeaders add(CharSequence header, CharSequence value) {
          nettyHeaders.add(header, value);
          return this;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1386: the fix leaves the no-argument constructor, so Netty's default header validation applies"
  lang java
  file http-netty/src/main/java/io/micronaut/http/netty/NettyHttpHeaders.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  package io.micronaut.http.netty;

  import io.micronaut.core.convert.ConversionService;
  import io.micronaut.http.MutableHttpHeaders;
  import io.netty.handler.codec.http.DefaultHttpHeaders;

  public class NettyHttpHeaders implements MutableHttpHeaders {

      io.netty.handler.codec.http.HttpHeaders nettyHeaders;
      final ConversionService<?> conversionService;

      public NettyHttpHeaders() {
          this.nettyHeaders = new DefaultHttpHeaders();
          this.conversionService = ConversionService.SHARED;
      }

      @Override
      public MutableHttpHeaders add(CharSequence header, CharSequence value) {
          nettyHeaders.add(header, value);
          return this;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1386: an encoder that builds a Netty header store and copies values into it without touching the validation flag is not reported"
  lang java
  file http-server-netty/src/main/java/io/micronaut/http/server/netty/encoders/HttpResponseEncoder.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  package io.micronaut.http.server.netty.encoders;

  import io.netty.handler.codec.http.DefaultHttpHeaders;
  import io.netty.handler.codec.http.HttpHeaders;

  public class HttpResponseEncoder {

      protected void encode(MutableHttpResponse<?> response) {
          io.netty.handler.codec.http.HttpHeaders nettyHeaders = new DefaultHttpHeaders();
          for (Map.Entry<String, List<String>> entry : response.getHeaders()) {
              nettyHeaders.set(entry.getKey(), entry.getValue());
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1386: a header store constructed with validation explicitly enabled is not reported"
  lang java
  file http-netty/src/main/java/io/micronaut/http/netty/NettyHttpParameters.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  package io.micronaut.http.netty;

  import io.netty.handler.codec.http.DefaultHttpHeaders;

  public class NettyHttpParameters {

      public io.netty.handler.codec.http.HttpHeaders validatingHeaders() {
          return new DefaultHttpHeaders(true);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1386: a boolean header written through a validating store is not read as the validation flag"
  lang java
  file http-netty/src/main/java/io/micronaut/http/netty/NettyHttpResponseFactory.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  package io.micronaut.http.netty;

  import io.netty.handler.codec.http.DefaultHttpHeaders;
  import io.netty.handler.codec.http.HttpHeaders;

  public class NettyHttpResponseFactory {

      HttpHeaders headers() {
          return new DefaultHttpHeaders().setBoolean("x-cache-hit", false);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1386: an HTTP/2 codec builder that turns the documented header-validation flag off"
  lang java
  file http-server-netty/src/main/java/io/micronaut/http/server/netty/http2/Http2ServerHandler.java
  expect VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  package io.micronaut.http.server.netty.http2;

  import io.netty.handler.codec.http2.Http2FrameCodec;
  import io.netty.handler.codec.http2.Http2FrameCodecBuilder;

  public class Http2ServerHandler {

      Http2FrameCodec codec() {
          return Http2FrameCodecBuilder.forServer()
                  .validateHeaders(false)
                  .build();
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1386: the same builder left at its validating default is not reported"
  lang java
  file http-server-netty/src/main/java/io/micronaut/http/server/netty/http2/Http2ServerHandler.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  package io.micronaut.http.server.netty.http2;

  import io.netty.handler.codec.http2.Http2FrameCodec;
  import io.netty.handler.codec.http2.Http2FrameCodecBuilder;

  public class Http2ServerHandler {

      Http2FrameCodec codec() {
          return Http2FrameCodecBuilder.forServer()
                  .validateHeaders(true)
                  .autoAckSettingsFrame(false)
                  .build();
      }
  }
  ```
